Mass and global energy residuals are approximately machine precision. The
maximum pressure-equalization error is 0.00611. Cold and hot isothermality
indicators are 0.0313 and 0.0347 respectively.

== Mandatory limitations ==

* The physical-validity verdict is '''indeterminate''': Mach number is
  unavailable until actual passage areas are supplied.
* The observed passive-valve chronology is '''non-nominal''' and contains a
  repeated transition. This behavior is simulated rather than suppressed.
* The ideal-air model fixes Z = 1 and constant heat capacities.
* The configured humid-air screen predicts condensation or frost risk in S, L
  and C. It does not model removal of water or the resulting dry-gas cycle.
* UA, CdA, exchanger pressure loss, pump power, mechanical friction and
  transmission efficiency require hardware-level validation.
* The quoted 110.21 W is thermodynamic input to the gas, not guaranteed pedal
  input at the crank.

== Reproduction ==

The configuration is
<code>examples/cooling_cell_x2_reference.toml</code>. The result was generated
with version 0.1.0 of the Python DADA engine solver using SI units and a
successive-cycle periodic-state search.

<syntaxhighlight lang="console">
python -m dada_solver.cli examples/cooling_cell_x2_reference.toml \
  --plot outputs/publication_cooling_cell_x2_cycle.png

python -m dada_solver.mechanism_animation \
  examples/cooling_cell_x2_reference.toml \
  outputs/publication_cooling_cell_x2_mechanism.gif --frames 90 --fps 18
</syntaxhighlight>

